  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_020: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.6352 acc / 0.6183 F1 at 7.02 GPU hrs. PCA clearly outperforms scgpt (0.629 vs 0.518), and weighted fusion slightly edges out concat. The major untested dimension with the best-known settings is the profile aggregation method (avgpool vs transformer). Question: config_022 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a single-variable change from the current best, testing whether transformer-based aggregation across multiple profiles captures inter-profile interactions that simple average pooling misses. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-potential-impact knob remaining. Rationale: With 5 experiments left after this one, exploiting the proven backbone (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted) while probing the one untested structural change (transformer aggregation) is the most efficient path to either confirm avgpool suffices or discover a meaningful accuracy gain. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds self-attention layers over profiles, so I estimate ~8–10 GPU hrs (moderately higher than the 7.02 for avgpool+weighted), which is acceptable given its potential to unlock the best configuration."
